# Binaries
bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Compiled command binaries. `go build` with no -o writes the binary next to
# the package it built, so a build run from a cmd/ directory — or a
# `go build -o <name>` in the repo root — leaves a ~100 MB artifact that is
# easy to `git add -A` by accident and impossible to remove from history
# afterwards. Name each cmd target rather than globbing: an entry like
# `/agent` would also ignore a future source directory of that name.
/codecov
/decisionbox-api
/decisionbox-agent
/services/api/api
/services/agent/agent
/services/agent/validation-replay

# Go
vendor/
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

